      "content": "My apologies for the confusion. Let's get straight to the point with the facts about transit and entry visas:\n\n1. **Singapore**: Upon arrival, you will need an Entry Visa. This visa permits you to stay in Singapore for up to 90 days. Ensure your passports are valid for at least six months beyond your stay.\n\n2. **Vietnam**: For your layover in Vietnam, you will need a Transit Visa. This visa allows you to stay in Vietnam for up to 24 hours, which should be sufficient time to catch your connecting flight. Make sure your passports are valid for at least six months beyond your stay.\n\n3. **Thailand**: When you land in Thailand, you will need an Entry Visa again. This visa allows you to stay in Thailand for up to 30 days. Ensure your passports are still valid for at least six months beyond your stay.\n\nIn summary, an Entry Visa is required for each country you intend to stay in for more than 24 hours, while a Transit Visa is needed for short layovers (up to 24 hours) when you're merely passing through a country on your way to another destination. Make sure all your documents are in order to avoid any goblin-like complications at the border!",
